module gunbc.plans.fleet_machine_naming

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { h2, h3, p, li, li_blocks, ul, ol, quote }

fn fleet_machine_naming_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    quote(blocks: [
      p(text: "**Goal:** each machine has one internal name, and every other name it answers to is derived from that one root: hostname, runner labels and registration names, BMC secret ids, `/etc/gunbc` paths, known_hosts entries, LAN and tailnet names. One physical board gets one identity, keyed by its board serial, and a second identity on an observed serial refuses. **Method:** `gunbc.design_argument::single_authority`, `gunbc.design_argument::root_generalization` and `gunbc.design_argument::replacement_migration` (the gap-intolerant carve-out for srv1-srv4, which serve the required job). **Standing:** the operator answered D1-D10 on 2026-11-10 (section 8), and the program may proceed in the PR order of section 6. Each host's flip is still its own PR and live window."),
      p(text: "**Operator direction (2026-11-10):** one internal name per machine, which is the root. The hostname is downstream of that name and never authored beside it. srv1-srv4 and mtcollins1 are renamed with names drawn by `gunbc.hostname_allocation` `draw_human_name` over `gunbc.host_names.gen_z`, with the entropy recorded as the receipt. The Sparks (srv9-srv12), mtjade1, the Hetzner guests and the H11 host each converge on one name. Duplicates are removed: srv13 and srv15 are one board (kept as bobo); srv16 is a reserved key with no board."),
      p(text: "**Read at:** gunbc main `b687f96f16bd` (census) and `b3c701d554f0` (plan). The two revisions differ by two commits that touch no file read here."),
    ]),

    h2(text: "1. Displaced cost"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "Each machine is restated in at least seven lists written by hand and keyed by `HostIdentity`: `gunbc.fleet.fleet_host_identity` `operator_hosts`, `gunbc.hostname_allocation` `gunbc_fleet_hostname_allocations`, `gunbc.fleet.fleet_enrollment` `fleet_enrollment_intents`, `gunbc.fleet.machine_board` `machine_board_rows`, `gunbc.fleet.fleet_asset_identity` `chassis_srvN`, `gunbc.runner.runner_host_deploy` `runner_host_spec_rows`, and `gunbc.fleet.fleet_host_key_enrollment` `fleet_host_key_enrollments`. Adding or renaming a machine means editing every one of them, and a forgotten one fails silently. Example: `gunbc.runner.runner_connectivity_recovery` `PerHostReplaceBudgetState` returns 0 for any host outside srv1-srv4."),
      li(text: "The serial-keyed refusal already exists but the fleet roster does not consume it. `gunbc.machine_intake.subject` `bind_unit_key` refuses `BoardSerialDuplicatedAcrossUnits`. The fleet joins identity to unit only through `gunbc.fleet.fleet_host_backing` `HostBacking.unit`, and only for enrolled rows: srv1-srv4 are `Absent` (serial never read) and srv13/srv15 are not enrolled. Two identities for one board therefore entered twice: srv14 and host-94c81d (deleted 2026-11-05), and srv13 and srv15 (`gunbc.integration_concern::srv13_and_srv15_name_one_board`)."),
      li(text: "Hostnames already diverge from identities for eight hosts: srv9-srv12, srv14, srv15, mtjade1 and host-6ce85c. Thirteen production sites compare the kernel hostname to the identity string without a lookup (section 4.4, class b*), so on those hosts they refuse or misbind today."),
    ]),

    h2(text: "2. Target model"),
    h3(text: "2.1 One machine row, one root"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**One machine row per physical unit.** It lives in `gunbc.fleet.fleet_host_identity`, which already holds the `HostIdentity` authority. The row has two parts. `name` is the drawn `gunbc.hostname_allocation` `HumanName` plus its `HumanNameDraw` receipt; the H11 and any other undrawn legacy spelling is `LegacyHostname`. `unit` is a `MachineUnit`, either `OwnedBoard { serial: BoardSerialObservation list | SerialUnread { read_obligation } }` or `ProviderInstance { resource: ProviderResourceBinding }`. The row reuses `gunbc.machine_intake.subject` `BoardSerialObservation` and `gunbc.fleet.fleet_host_backing` `ProviderResourceBinding` rather than minting either again."),
      li(text: "**The identity is the rendered name, not a second spelling of it.** `HostIdentity` changes from a branded `NonEmptyStr` to `sole_constructor`, minted only by the roster admission (2.2) as the canonical rendering of `name` (`human_name_canonical_hostname`). Today any `\"srv1\" as HostIdentity` cast mints an identity. Afterwards no accepted program can, which is the wall this plan climbs to (2.4). This reverses `gunbc.hostname_allocation` `gunbc_hostname_allocation_scope_disposition`, which calls deriving a hostname from the identity nicknaming. Its objection holds only for a hostname that coincides with how an opaque string is spelled. Here the identity carries the typed name, and rendering it is a declared, total, exact function. The opaque-identity rule of 2026-10-07 still holds: a drawn name encodes no provider, architecture, role or rack. Decision D1."),
      li(text: "**The roster is derived from the rows.** `operator_hosts` becomes the admitted roster's population, not a second list. `gunbc_fleet_hostname_allocations` is retired: what is left of it is each row's draw receipt. `machine_board_rows`, `fleet_enrollment_intents` and `runner_host_spec_rows` stay as separate facts, but each is keyed by an admitted identity and holds only its own columns. The same climb was made for instrument targets in `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode::a_target_roster_restates_the_labels_its_bindings_name`."),
      li(text: "**`PhysicalAssetIdentity` `chassis-srvN` stays a separate concern.** A chassis is a physical container whose board can be swapped, so it is not the machine identity. Its spelling embeds a host name, though, and gets the opaque treatment `gpu_board_NN` already has. Decision D6."),
    ]),
    h3(text: "2.2 Admission: one identity per board"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "`admit_fleet_machines(rows)` folds the rows through `std.allocation_roster` `build_allocation_roster`. The primary key is the rendered name, so a name claimed twice refuses with `AllocationPrimaryKeyRepeated`. The secondary key is the unit key: the bound `UnitKey` for an owned board, or the provider resource id for a guest."),
      li(text: "The serial axis reuses `bind_unit_key`, with `other_units` set to the keys already bound by earlier rows. A second row on an observed serial refuses `BoardSerialDuplicatedAcrossUnits { serial }` and names both rows. Contradictory serial readings refuse `BoardSerialContradictory`. A row whose serial has never been read carries its read obligation and claims no key: it is not refused and not counted as unique. This follows `gunbc.design_argument::epistemic_humility`, and the refusal applies on an observed serial, as asked."),
      li(text: "The H11 host's intake rows are keyed by BMC MAC (`supermicro_h11ssl_unit1_*`). They join through the same unit key once the board serial is read. A MAC is not the key."),
    ]),
    h3(text: "2.3 Every derived name and its one derivation site"),
    p(text: "Each function takes the admitted machine (or its `HostIdentity`) and nothing hand-spelled. Where a function already exists it is kept and its callers converge on it; `(new)` marks the ones to add."),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Linux hostname:** `gunbc.fleet.fleet_naming` `linux_hostname` (exists; re-keyed from the allocation to the machine row). `hostnamectl` desired state comes from it through `gunbc.deployed_intent_v1` `deployed_intent_v1_from_fleet_slot`."),
      li(text: "**Runner host label:** `gunbc.runner.runner_slot_allocation` `runner_host_label` (exists, `host as String`). It stays correct unchanged once the identity is the name. The six direct `host as String` label sites in `gunbc.fleet.fleet_converge_workflow` (gcp-iam, arrival-converge, printer, gcp-iam bootstrap, mtcollins1-boot) move onto it."),
      li(text: "**Runner registration names:** `gunbc.build_cache.build_cache_instance` `runner_slot_instance_name_prefix` (exists). `gunbc.build_cache.build_cache_latency_probe` `host_from_runner_name`'s literal `srvN-` prefixes are deleted in favour of `gunbc.runner.runner_incarnation` `parse_jit_registration_name` over the roster."),
      li(text: "**BMC secret ids:** `bmc_admin_secret_id(machine)` (new, lifted from `gunbc.bmc.bmc_onboarding` `altra_onboarding_plan`'s concat) and `gunbc.bmc.bmc_health_reader` `bmc_health_reader_secret_id` (exists). Each returns a branded id that the IAM binding rows in `gunbc.assimilate.bmc_token_federation` and `gunbc.auth.fleet_secret_accessor_roster` consume, replacing the literals `bmc-srv3-admin`, `bmc-srv4-admin`, `bmc-mtcollins1-gunbc` and `bmc-mtjade1-gunbc`. The same derivation covers the host-named non-BMC secrets: `mtcollins1-ssh-host-key` and `gunbc-srv4-strata-api-key`. Decision D4."),
      li(text: "**`/etc/gunbc` per-host paths:** `bmc_known_hosts_path(machine)` and `bmc_identity_path(machine)` (new, in `gunbc.host.host_layout`). They replace the four literals in `gunbc.bmc.bmc_fan_converge`. The converge receipt path (`fleet_converge_receipt_dir`) is already derived."),
      li(text: "**known_hosts address:** `gunbc.fleet.fleet_host_key_enrollment` rows are keyed by `HostIdentity` and get their address from `fleet_lan_name(machine)` / `fleet_tailnet_name(machine)`. The literal `\"srvN\" as HostIdentity` and `labels: [\"srvN\"]` are deleted."),
      li(text: "**LAN name:** `fleet_lan_name(machine)` (new, in `gunbc.host.host_name_resolution`) is the label plus `lan_zone_wire`. It replaces `srv2_lan_name_under` and the `as String as DnsLabel` casts in `gunbc.host.boot_medium`."),
      li(text: "**Tailnet name:** `gunbc.fleet.fleet_tailnet` `tailnet_host_from` (exists), re-typed to take the machine. The `srv1.tailecbe08.ts.net` and `srv2...` literals in `gunbc.auth.tracker_web_oauth_client` and `gunbc.serving.router_dev_policy` move onto it."),
      li(text: "**SSH target:** `gunbc.runner.runner_host_deploy` `RunnerHostSpec.ssh_target` is derived as `<listener account>@<gunbc.fleet.fleet_intent_network host_lan_address(host)>`. `host_label` is deleted (it is `runner_host_label`). The users come from the fleet-wide account (the gunbc-runner cutover), so each row keeps only real overrides. `gunbc.fleet.fleet_reach_endpoint` `fleet_owned_probe_endpoint_for`, which today reaches a host at its bare identity string, resolves through `fleet_lan_name`."),
      li(text: "**Router DNS:** not authored. The CR1000A publishes the DHCP client hostname (option 12), so the LAN name follows the Linux hostname once the lease renews; this explains why srv14 does not resolve while butch does. The model reads it (`gunbc.network_identity_subsumption`) and does not write it. The MAC-to-IP reservation is keyed by MAC and survives a rename."),
    ]),
    h3(text: "2.4 The rule a witness enforces, and its authorable reds"),
    ul(items: [
      li_blocks(blocks: [
        p(text: "**W1, carrier (structurally guaranteed).** Planted rows reach `admit_fleet_machines`:"),
        ul(items: [
          li(text: "Two rows reading serial `BR80S6102300049` refuse `BoardSerialDuplicatedAcrossUnits` naming both. This is the srv13/srv15 shape, built as a fixture."),
          li(text: "Two rows rendering `bobo` refuse `AllocationPrimaryKeyRepeated`."),
          li(text: "A row with contradictory FRU and SMBIOS serials refuses."),
          li(text: "A row with `SerialUnread` admits and carries its obligation."),
          li(text: "Positive control: the production rows admit."),
        ]),
      ]),
      li(text: "**W2, derivation by execution.** A fixture machine is admitted under name A and again under name B. Every 2.3 function, run through its real producer (the emitted fleet-converge `host` options, the onboarding plan's credential ref, the known_hosts anchor rows, the RunnerHostSpec lookup), yields A-forms under A and B-forms under B, and no output contains the other name. Deleting any one site's derivation (restoring a literal) makes that site's B-row fail. This is the discriminating red, and it is an inhabitance claim on the real path (`gunbc.design_argument::witness_one_interface`)."),
      li(text: "**W3, the wall (structurally impossible for identity minting).** Fixture source `data x: HostIdentity = \"srv1\"` and `\"srv1\" as HostIdentity` are handed to the compiler and refuse, because `HostIdentity` is `sole_constructor`. The positive control compiles the production roster."),
      li(text: "**Honest ceiling.** A derived name typed as a free `String` (an argv word, a prose receipt) can still be written as a literal anywhere. The types in 2.3 make the typed positions unwritable from literals; free text stays at review (mitigation). That residual is stated here and is not claimed as covered."),
    ]),

    h2(text: "3. Why the corpus forks: causes and root fixes"),
    p(text: "Classes are the brief's four: (1) missing generic carrier, (2) missing host-keyed lookup, (3) a literal instead of a derivation, (4) a leaf written before its second instance existed. Git history cannot order most of these: `fleet_compute_host_for_identity`, `host_lan_address`, `PerHostReplaceBudgetState` and most host modules trace to the import commit `364fcb5a8c23` (2026-09-19). The (4) readings therefore rest on structure and comments, except in the boot and arrival lane, where the dates show the generic came first."),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**`gunbc.srv3.srv3_boot_once_cd`: (2) plus (3).** A Redfish boot-once PATCH and ForceRestart, hard-coding `srv3_onboarding_plan` and `/tmp/srv3_*.json`. It ignores `plan.redfish_system_id`. Its subject, scopes and attempt live in `srv3_os_install_actuate_workflow`. The generic parts already exist: `altra_onboarding_plan(host, bmc_host)` with rows for srv1-srv4, and `ActuatorBootOnce` / `boot_once_step` in `gunbc.nbd_proxy_virtual_media_install`. That realization itself hard-codes `BmcController { node: srv3_host }`. What is missing is `onboarding_plan_for(host)`. All of `dag/gunbc/srv3/` (14 modules) and `dag/test/claim/srv3/` (26 witnesses) are one host's copy of a lane that srv1, srv2, srv4 and bobo need too."),
      li(text: "**`gunbc.auth.branch_dispatch_federation` `mtcollins1_boot_run_scoped_federation_for`: (3) plus (4).** It copies `fleet_run_scoped_federation`'s body field by field, with literal labels and service-account ids, and `boot_federation_names` is an `if host == mtcollins1` lookup. Both were written 2026-10-10, after the generic `gunbc.host.managed_host_boot_federation` (2026-10-03)."),
      li(text: "**`gunbc.machine_intake.arrival_subject`: (4) plus (1).** The row has `wire: \"mtjade1\"` (a string, not a `HostIdentity`) and no grant field. Admission hard-wires `mtjade1_live_standing_grant` and the mtcollins1 exclusion. The module says itself that a second row would refuse until the fold joins each row to its own grant. srv13's identity-bind inputs are already waiting as that second row."),
      li(text: "**`gunbc.runner.runner_connectivity_recovery` `PerHostReplaceBudgetState`: (1).** Fixed fields `srv1..srv4: Int`, with four-arm get and decrement chains. Any other host silently gets a budget of 0. `git grep 'Map<HostIdentity'` finds nothing, so no host-keyed carrier exists. The same file's `host_reach_admission_for_fleet_host` (`if srv3 || srv4` refuse) is (3)."),
      li(text: "**`RunnerHostSpec` rows: (3).** The four rows have identical users and app, a `host_label` that duplicates the identity, and an `ssh_target` IP that duplicates `gunbc.fleet.fleet_intent_network` (which `host_lan_address(host)` already derives). `gunbc.fleet.print_converge` and `gunbc.runner.runner_capacity_operator_access` bypass the `runner_host_spec_for` lookup, and the latter falls back to the literal `briansrls`."),
      li(text: "**Host-equality branches: (2) and (3).** These are four-arm chains that exist where a lookup already does. Examples: `gunbc.fleet.fleet_show_effective_read` `fleet_host_control_plane` beside `fleet_compute_host_for_identity`, and `gunbc.host.host_toolchain_ensure` `host_toolchain_direct_access`. Others are per-host policy written as literals: `gunbc.host.host_converge` `if host == operator_host_srv3 { FreshStandup }`, and `gunbc.host.host_memory_observation` `gunbc_ci_host_fixed_overhead_for`."),
      li(text: "**The common upstream cause:** the identity is a free string any site may cast, and there is no per-machine row to hang a column on. The cheapest local move is therefore always `if host == X` or a new `X_`-prefixed declaration. Each such leaf is `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode::a_rule_is_applied_at_the_site_that_prompted_it_and_not_its_sibling`. Each kernel-hostname-equals-identity comparison is `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode::symptom_link_patched_without_the_earliest_unjustified_boundary`: the earliest unjustified link is the unmodeled identity-to-hostname relation, not the comparator."),
    ]),
    h3(text: "3.1 Root fixes, ranked by the forks they stop"),
    ol(items: [
      li(text: "**R1, the machine row and the sole_constructor identity (2.1-2.2).** This stops new identity literals, second identities for one board, and new per-host lists, which become columns keyed by an admitted identity."),
      li(text: "**R2, one host-keyed record lookup.** `fleet_host_record_for(host) -> FleetHostRecord?` joins the compute host, baseboard, deploy access, ssh transport, `BmcOnboardingPlan` and `RunnerHostSpec`. It absorbs `host_toolchain_direct_access`, `fleet_host_control_plane`, `fleet_host_ssh_transport`, the `briansrls` fallback, the direct `srvN_runner_host_spec` and `srvN_onboarding_plan` imports, and the `srv3_host` target in the nbd-proxy realization."),
      li(text: "**R3, a host-keyed total map.** Search `std.allocation_roster`, which already holds a keyed map, before minting `HostKeyed<T>`: a total get, update and fold over the admitted roster. It absorbs `PerHostReplaceBudgetState`, `materialized_width_for_host`, `gunbc_ci_host_fixed_overhead_for` and the 11 branches in `host_memory_observation`, and it ends the silent zero for hosts outside srv1-srv4."),
      li(text: "**R4, per-host policy as row fields** on `gunbc.fleet.fleet_enrollment` `HostEnrollmentIntent`: apply mode, reach admission, arrival standing grant, run-scoped federation names. It absorbs `host_reach_admission_for_fleet_host`, `arrival_subject`'s grant and exclusion, and `mtcollins1_boot_run_scoped_federation_for` (routed through `fleet_run_scoped_federation`), and it admits srv13/bobo's arrival as a second row."),
      li(text: "**R5, a host-generic Redfish boot-once: delivered by smart-crane-730, not built here.** smart-crane-730's bobo PR 2 deletes `gunbc.srv3.srv3_boot_once_cd`, `srv3_os_install_actuate_workflow` and `srv3_bmc_credential_resolve`. It replaces them with a host-generic Redfish boot-once (target Pxe or Cd, scopes rooted at the managed host's bound controller, gated on the PXE edge holding a binding for that NIC) and a fleet-converge mode, `managed_host_network_install` (smart-crane-730, 2026-11-10). This plan consumes that result and adds no boot-once work. The srv3 literals that remain after it lands (BMC secret refs, `/etc/gunbc` paths in `bmc_fan_converge`) are handled by P4's derivations."),
      li(text: "**Review tell, not a new gate or census:** a production declaration or file whose name embeds a machine name, or a new `host == operator_host_X` arm, is a presumption of fork. The author answers why it should not be generalized, or names the trigger for doing so (`gunbc.design_argument::root_generalization`)."),
    ]),

    h2(text: "4. Fork census at grain"),
    p(text: "All counts were taken at `b687f96f16bd` over `dag src/v2` with bounded `git grep` plus source inspection. A negative match is not proof that nothing exists, and no census instrument is proposed. The test witnesses were inspected only where a search surfaced them."),
    h3(text: "4.1 Identity string literals"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "Command: `git grep -oF '\"srvN\"' -- dag src/v2 | wc -l` (exact), plus an embedded-literal regex `'\"[^\"]*\\bsrvN\\b[^\"]*\"'`. The regex can span two adjacent literals, so its counts are approximate."),
      li(text: "**Exact literals, production / test:** `\"srv1\"` 486 (56 / 430), `\"srv2\"` 192 (24 / 168), `\"srv3\"` 171 (35 / 136), `\"srv4\"` 112 (30 / 82), `\"mtcollins1\"` 174 (7 / 167)."),
      li(text: "**Embedded literals (not exact):** 1616, 314, 1095, 425 and 613 respectively."),
      li(text: "**Disposition: derive** for production live-path literals (examples: `gunbc.ci.ci_budget_tree`, `gunbc.fabric.fabric_writer_roster`, `gunbc.fleet.fleet_multi_principal_probe`, `gunbc.host.host_reach_identity_probe`, `gunbc.fabric.workspace_source` `workspace_source_pack_host`)."),
      li(text: "**Disposition: keep** for historical observations: a captured hostname, a receipt line, an `artifacts/` path. They record what was seen on a date, and rewriting them would fabricate history (decision D7)."),
      li(text: "**Disposition: generalize** for test fixtures that test a generic rule. They move to fixture identities minted through the admission, so they stop asserting a real host's name."),
      li(text: "**Unknown:** the split of the embedded literals between live-path and historical."),
    ]),
    h3(text: "4.2 Per-host branches"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "Command: `git grep -nE '(==|!=) *\\(?operator_host_[a-z0-9]+|host_identity_eq\\([^)]*operator_host_[a-z0-9]+' -- dag src/v2`."),
      li(text: "Result: 279 lines in 94 files. runner 20/6, host 31/10, fleet 31/7. Top modules: `host_memory_observation` 11, `runner_connectivity_recovery` 10, `fleet_runner_connectivity` 8, `fleet_show_effective_read` 8. The brief's regex also misses the common `(host as String) == (operator_host_srvN as String)` form."),
      li(text: "**Disposition: generalize** through R2-R4. A branch that selects a per-host fact becomes a lookup; a branch that encodes per-host policy becomes a row field."),
      li(text: "**Unknown:** the arms written as string comparisons against unquoted names."),
    ]),
    h3(text: "4.3 Declaration names embedding a machine"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "Command: `git grep -ohE '\\b(data|fn|type) +[A-Za-z0-9_]*(srv[0-9]+|mtcollins1|mtjade1|183527|3dde7f|6ce85c)[A-Za-z0-9_]*' -- dag src/v2 | wc -l`."),
      li(text: "Result: 2902 (1943 production, 959 test; 3021 case-insensitive). By host: mtcollins1 804, srv1 802, srv3 606, srv4 261, srv2 214, mtjade1 164, srv13 60, everything else at most 10 each."),
      li(text: "Top directories: `gunbc/machine_intake` 559, `gunbc/fleet` 379, `gunbc/host` 199, `gunbc/serving` 175, `gunbc/srv3` 134."),
      li(text: "167 files carry a machine name in their path (srv3 82, mtcollins1 75, srv1 22, mtjade1 16, h11ssl_unit 7)."),
      li(text: "**Disposition: generalize** for rules named after one host (the srv3 install lane, the mtcollins1 boot run and federation, `mtjade1` arrival, `srvN_onboarding_plan`, `srvN_runner_host_spec`)."),
      li(text: "**Disposition: re-key** for facts about one machine (its captures, its DIMM census, its first-contact readings). They are legitimately per machine, but by D2 they become rows in tables keyed by `HostIdentity` rather than declarations named after the machine, so a rename never touches them. The per-machine module directories (`machine_intake/mtcollins1_*`, `serving/srv1_*`) are generalized table by table as each one's rule is lifted."),
      li(text: "**Disposition: delete** for rows of retired identities (srv13 by the bobo lane, srv16)."),
      li(text: "**Unknown:** the per-declaration split between rule and fact. It is decided per PR, by `gunbc.design_argument::root_generalization` step 2."),
    ]),
    h3(text: "4.4 Derived-name sites"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "Classes: (a) derived through the allocation, (b) concatenated or cast from the identity string, (b*) kernel hostname compared to or cast into the identity with no lookup, (c) a hand literal."),
      li_blocks(blocks: [
        p(text: "**Hostname:**"),
        ul(items: [
          li(text: "(a), 8 sites: `deployed_intent_v1_from_fleet_slot`, `host_reset_return_run`, `host_reach_identity_probe`, `managed_host_unit_hold`, `network_identity_subsumption`, `workspace_allocation_supply`, `workspace_tool_observer`, `fleet_converge_cli` `converge_host_selector_identity`."),
          li(text: "(b*), 13 sites: `fabric_writer_identity_observe`, `host_memory_envelope_observe`, `runner_microvm_host_ready`, `runner_microvm_slot_controller`, `runner_microvm_network_converge`, `runner_microvm_network_apply`, `runner_service_slot_controller`, `workspace_host_offer_observe`, `approval_request_client` `classify_approval_origin`, `ci_deploy_target_host`, `runner_browser_toolchain`."),
          li(text: "(c), 2 sites: `workspace_source_pack_host`, `srv3_fleet_slot_host_name`."),
          li(text: "**Disposition: derive.** Every (b*) resolves through `resolve_host_selector` before the flip (P1). It refuses wrongly on renamed hosts today."),
        ]),
      ]),
      li(text: "**Runner labels and registration names:** (b) through `runner_host_label` and its six bypasses; (c) `host_from_runner_name` and the four `host_label` literals. **Disposition: derive.**"),
      li(text: "**BMC and host-named secrets:** (b) `altra_onboarding_plan`, `bmc_health_reader_secret_id`; (c) the `bmc_fan_converge` srv3/srv4 credential refs, `bmc_srv3_secret_name`, `srv3_os_install_actuate_*`, `mtcollins1_bmc_gunbc_secret_ref`, `mtjade1_bmc_gunbc_secret_ref`, the `bmc-mtcollins1` controller in `bmc_first_contact_reading`, `mtcollins1-ssh-host-key`, `gunbc-srv4-strata-api-key`. Command: `git grep -n 'bmc-srv\\|bmc-mtcollins'` gives 25 and 41 matches, most in artifacts and prose. **Disposition: derive.**"),
      li(text: "**`/etc/gunbc` paths:** (c), 4 in `bmc_fan_converge`. Command: `git grep -n '/etc/gunbc'` gives 120 matches, of which 5 carry a host. **Disposition: derive.**"),
      li(text: "**known_hosts:** (c) `fleet_host_key_enrollments` (srv1-srv4 and `srv1.tailecbe08.ts.net`, identity and label both hand-written). **Disposition: derive the address; the host key stays an observation.**"),
      li(text: "**LAN and tailnet:** (b) `srv2_lan_name_under`, `boot_medium`, `tailnet_host_from`; (c) the zones `mynetworksettings.com` and `tailecbe08.ts.net` (legitimate zone facts) and the `srv1/srv2.tailecbe08.ts.net` literals in `tracker_web_oauth_client` and `router_dev_policy`. Endpoint labels in `fleet_intent_network` (`srv1-host-lan` and others) are (c). **Disposition: derive.**"),
      li(text: "**SSH targets:** (c) the four `RunnerHostSpec.ssh_target`; (b) `fleet_owned_probe_endpoint_for` (bare identity as a DNS name, 7 callers); (c) the `node@srvN` rows in `fleet_shell_transport_observation`, which are historical observations and kept. **Disposition: derive.**"),
      li(text: "**Not host-named:** sccache endpoints and docker contexts (none found). The Rust seed constructs no names."),
    ]),
    h3(text: "4.5 Live artifacts"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "Each machine's `/etc/hostname` and kernel hostname."),
      li(text: "GitHub runner registrations. JIT `<identity>-NN-<epoch>-<pid>` names carry labels `[self-hosted, linux, arm64, <identity>, gunbc-heavy]`. The required `v2-bootstrap` job runs on `[self-hosted, linux, arm64]`, any fleet slot, with no host label. Six host-pinned job families in `.github/workflows/fleet-converge.yml` (75 `srvN` occurrences) are pinned to srv1 or `inputs.host`."),
      li(text: "Secret Manager: `bmc-srv3-admin`, `bmc-srv4-admin`, `bmc-<host>-health-reader`, `bmc-mtcollins1-gunbc`, `bmc-mtjade1-gunbc`, `mtcollins1-ssh-host-key`, `gunbc-srv4-strata-api-key`, plus their IAM grants. **Unknown:** whether `bmc-srv1-admin` and `bmc-srv2-admin` exist live. They are not modeled as grants."),
      li(text: "known_hosts anchors (`gunbc.fleet.fleet_known_hosts_anchor` over the enrollment rows)."),
      li(text: "Router DHCP option-12 names (read only)."),
      li(text: "Tailscale machine names. **Unknown:** whether they equal the identity or the hostname; the corpus has no observation."),
      li(text: "The OAuth client redirect URIs registered for `srv1/srv2.tailecbe08.ts.net`. These are outward-facing (decision D8)."),
      li(text: "`/etc/gunbc/bmc-known-hosts/srvN` and `/etc/gunbc/bmc-identities/srvN-machine-id` on srv3 and srv4."),
      li(text: "**Disposition:** each is produced from the 2.3 derivation by the modes in section 5, or recorded as a gap there."),
    ]),

    h2(text: "5. Staged cutover"),
    h3(text: "5.1 Modes that exist and gaps"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**Hostname set:** partial. `gunbc.host.host_effect` `SetHostnameCas`, realized by `gunbc.hostname_set` `hostname_set_cas` with read-back and a no-op re-run in `gunbc.host.host_identity_assimilation` `host_identity_converge_from_base`. Wet entries exist for srv1 and srv2 only. The stored baselines in `gunbc.deployed_intent_v0` are the pre-2026-07 names, so a three-way merge hits `ConflictPlan` until the baselines are re-adopted (`gunbc.host.host_identity_adopt`). **Gap:** no fleet-converge mode, and nothing for srv3, srv4 or mtcollins1. A mode run from a peer host is needed, because a host's own fleet-converge job is pinned to its label."),
      li(text: "**Runner re-registration:** exists. `runner_host_file_converge` leads to `gunbc.runner.runner_slot_actuation` `activate_runner_slot_over`, which mints each JIT registration with `runner_host_label(host)`. Labels follow the identity on the next mint, with no separate re-registration. Drain and restore: `gunbc.runner.runner_host_withdraw` and `runner_host_restore`. **Gap:** dead offline registrations under the old name have no sweep for JIT names (`gunbc.recurring_failure_mode::a_registration_name_model_drifts_from_the_name_the_runner_registers_under`)."),
      li(text: "**DNS:** none needed. It follows option 12 once the DHCP lease renews (2.3). The router transport is `WebUiManual`, so a reservation edit, if ever needed, is an operator step."),
      li(text: "**Secrets and IAM:** gap. `gunbc.auth.gcp_iam_converge` `GcpIamEffect` has only `CreateProvider` and `AddPolicyCells`, with no secret create and no removal. Bare secret creation exists only in `gunbc.auth.gcp_iam_bootstrap` `iam_bootstrap_ensure_bare_secret`, for grant-set secrets. The needed mode is a shadow copy: create `bmc-<new>-admin`, copy the latest version, and add the same cells, all additive. Retirement of the old secret follows `gunbc.bmc` rotation's derived published-credential retirement (#15317)."),
      li(text: "**known_hosts:** partial. `fleet_host_key_scan_wet` and `fleet_host_key_enroll_wet` are wired in `gunbc.ci.ci_spec`, but no mode calls them. Re-enrollment is a row under the new name with the same host key (additive). The anchor's `known_hosts_endpoint_conflict` catches a mismatch."),
      li(text: "**Listener account `briansrls` to `gunbc-runner`:** owned by cool-lark-40. Today it exists only for image-baked hosts (`gunbc.runner.runner_host_listener_account`). No converge exists for the SSH-applied srv1-srv4."),
      li(text: "**Board serial read:** the srv1-srv4 serials are unread (`fleet_host_backing` `HostUnitUnobserved`). The producer is `gunbc.machine_intake.arrival_converge` `identity_bind_provisional` (FRU plus SMBIOS), which already ran for mtcollins1 and mtjade1."),
    ]),
    h3(text: "5.2 Stages"),
    ol(items: [
      li(text: "**S0, model (no live change).** P1-P7 and P11 (section 6). Identity values do not change, so labels, secrets and hostnames are untouched. CI: unchanged; v2-bootstrap is unaffected. Rollback: revert."),
      li(text: "**S1, per host: serial read.** `identity_bind_provisional` runs for the host and its `SerialUnread` becomes observations; W1 then covers it. A refusal here stops that host's cutover (the line stops). CI: unchanged."),
      li_blocks(blocks: [
        p(text: "**S2, per host: shadow, additive.**"),
        ul(items: [
          li(text: "Create secrets under the new name, with IAM cells."),
          li(text: "Add known_hosts rows under the new name."),
          li(text: "Register the new Tailscale name and the OAuth redirect URIs if the host has them."),
          li(text: "Re-adopt the hostname baseline."),
        ]),
        p(text: "Old artifacts stay valid. CI: unchanged. Rollback: delete the new artifacts."),
      ]),
      li_blocks(blocks: [
        p(text: "**S3, per host: the flip, one window.**"),
        ul(items: [
          li(text: "`runner_host_withdraw` drains the host."),
          li(text: "The flip PR changes that one row's name to its accepted draw; generated workflows regenerate."),
          li(text: "The peer-run hostname mode sets and reads back the new hostname."),
          li(text: "In the same window, the host moves to `gunbc-runner` (cool-lark-40's cutover), so its live state changes once."),
          li(text: "`runner_host_file_converge` and `runner_host_restore` bring it back; the next JIT mints carry the new label."),
          li(text: "A DHCP renew updates the router name; `network_identity_subsumption` reads it back."),
        ]),
        p(text: "CI: the required pool loses that host's slots for the window. Host-pinned fleet-converge jobs for that host queue until its runners return under the new label. Rollback until S4: revert the flip PR and run the hostname mode back. Runners re-mint under the old label, and the old secrets and known_hosts rows still exist."),
      ]),
      li(text: "**S4, per host: retire the old name, piece by piece** (operator, D10): no fixed soak. Each old artifact is retired once the host has run on the new name and that artifact has no remaining reader, and whatever breaks is fixed at its derivation, not patched at the symptom. The artifacts: the old secrets (disabled, then deleted on the rotation route's retirement), the old known_hosts rows, the offline registrations, the old OAuth redirect URIs and the old Tailscale name. Rollback from here is a forward rename."),
    ]),
    h3(text: "5.3 Order across hosts (runner capacity)"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**srv4 first** (operator, D9: srv3 or srv4 first, the others once that works). srv3 waits on smart-crane-730's boot-once replacement (R5), so srv4 is the first flip. It serves at least 7 GitHub slots (memory admission up to 17); srv3 and srv1 keep serving v2-bootstrap through its window."),
      li(text: "**Then, once srv4 works end to end:** srv3 (after R5 and P4), srv2 (no established runner width, so its flip costs v2-bootstrap nothing), and srv1. srv1 hosts the srv1-pinned jobs (gcp-iam, mtcollins1-boot, arrival-converge, printer) and the fabric and revision slots; after P4 those jobs derive their label, so they follow the flip with no edit."),
      li(text: "**mtcollins1 at any point after srv4.** It is image-baked, already uses `gunbc-runner`, and takes 5 slots. Its flip changes the image's baked label, so the next image build carries it."),
      li(text: "**Then the hosts whose names are already drawn**, with no draw needed and the identity set to the drawn name: the Sparks srv9-srv12 (francis, emerson, mil, bastien), mtjade1 (eric), host-183527 (damien), host-3dde7f (gus), host-6ce85c (h11-a16, legacy). srv14 becomes butch in cool-lark-40's enrollment window (kept as is until this plan lands), and srv15 becomes bobo after smart-crane-730's admission has deleted srv13."),
    ]),

    h2(text: "6. PR sequence, with acceptance and completion"),
    p(text: "Each PR names its scope, what must execute for it to be accepted, and what is true when it is done. Program completion is the retirement condition at the end of this plan. The critical path to the first flip (srv4) is P1, P2, P3, P4, P5 and P7a-P7c. P6 and P11 run beside it."),
    ol(items: [
      li_blocks(blocks: [
        p(text: "**P0, this plan** (gunbc#16252, small)."),
        ul(items: [
          li(text: "**Acceptance:** `plan_documentation_wet` renders it, and `test.claim.plan_lens_witness` passes 5/5 with it registered. Both have been run."),
          li(text: "**Done:** merged."),
        ]),
      ]),
      li_blocks(blocks: [
        p(text: "**P1, the b* comparators** (small-medium; no dependency, so it can land first)."),
        ul(items: [
          li(text: "**Scope:** the 13 sites of 4.4 that compare or cast `hostname -s` against the identity resolve it through `gunbc.hostname_allocation` `resolve_host_selector` instead. This fixes misbinding that is live today on the eight hosts whose hostname differs from their identity."),
          li(text: "**Acceptance:** per site, a fixture host whose hostname differs from its identity (the srv14/butch shape) resolves to that identity, and an unknown hostname refuses with a typed cause. At least one site is exercised on its real producer path, `gunbc.ci.ci_deploy_target_host` `deploy_target_runner_identity_proves_host` with an observed `butch`. Generated workflows are byte-identical. v2-bootstrap is green."),
          li(text: "**Done:** a bounded `git grep` for `hostname_short_read(` and `as HostIdentity` over the 4.4 sites finds no comparison that skips the selector. The command and its hits are cited in the PR body."),
        ]),
      ]),
      li_blocks(blocks: [
        p(text: "**P2, the machine roster** (medium). Depends on smart-crane-730's bobo admission PR having deleted srv13."),
        ul(items: [
          li(text: "**Why the dependency:** srv13 and srv15 carry the same serial (BR80S6102300049), so landing first would refuse the production roster."),
          li_blocks(blocks: [
            p(text: "**Scope:**"),
            ul(items: [
              li(text: "The machine row (2.1) and `MachineUnit`; `admit_fleet_machines` (2.2) over `std.allocation_roster` and `bind_unit_key`."),
              li(text: "`operator_hosts` derived from the admitted rows. `gunbc_fleet_hostname_allocations` deleted, each row carrying its own name and draw receipt."),
              li(text: "A row's accepted-but-not-applied next draw as its own field (`next_name`), which is where srv1-4's and mtcollins1's draws live until their flips."),
              li(text: "The scope disposition rewritten (D1); srv16 deleted (D5); `chassis-srvN` made opaque (D6)."),
              li(text: "Serials seeded from the readings already in tree (mtcollins1, mtjade1, srv14, srv15); everything else `SerialUnread` with its obligation."),
            ]),
          ]),
          li_blocks(blocks: [
            p(text: "**Acceptance:**"),
            ul(items: [
              li(text: "W1's five cases (2.4), the duplicate-serial red included."),
              li(text: "The draw witness re-draws every receipt, the five accepted next draws included, in draw order, and gets the recorded name."),
              li(text: "No identity value changes, so every generated workflow is byte-identical and v2-bootstrap is green."),
            ]),
          ]),
          li(text: "**Done:** no hand-written roster list and no hostname rows remain. `fleet_host_backing`'s `unit` reads from the machine row, not a second copy."),
        ]),
      ]),
      li_blocks(blocks: [
        p(text: "**P3, serial reads** (small; live and read-only)."),
        ul(items: [
          li(text: "**Scope:** `gunbc.machine_intake.arrival_converge` `identity_bind_provisional` (FRU plus SMBIOS) runs for srv1-srv4, the Sparks and the H11, and the observations are recorded on the rows."),
          li(text: "**Acceptance:** each read either becomes observations on its row with W1's production control still admitting, or a refusal (duplicate or contradictory) stops that host's cutover. Nothing is written to any host."),
          li(text: "**Done:** every owned machine flipped in P8-P9 has an observed serial."),
        ]),
      ]),
      li_blocks(blocks: [
        p(text: "**P4, derivations** (medium-large)."),
        ul(items: [
          li(text: "**Scope:** the 2.3 functions; each (b) and (c) live-path site of 4.4 moves onto them, secret ids and IAM binding rows included."),
          li_blocks(blocks: [
            p(text: "**Acceptance:**"),
            ul(items: [
              li(text: "W2: a fixture machine renamed from A to B changes every producer's output, and no A-form survives. Restoring any one literal reds that site's row."),
              li(text: "With today's names, generated workflows and secret ids are byte-identical, so nothing changes behaviour yet."),
            ]),
          ]),
          li(text: "**Done:** the 4.4 kinds have one derivation site each. Remaining literal names are only historical observations (D7), shown by a bounded `git grep` per kind (`bmc-srv`, `/etc/gunbc/.*srv`, `tailecbe08`, `briansrls@`) cited in the PR body."),
        ]),
      ]),
      li_blocks(blocks: [
        p(text: "**P5, machine handles** (large, mechanical; the cost of D11)."),
        ul(items: [
          li(text: "**Scope:** the per-machine symbols `operator_host_srv1` (950 references) and the rest become stable opaque handles, so that a later rename edits only the name field of one row."),
          li(text: "**Acceptance:** no value changes, generated workflows are byte-identical, and the compiler resolves every reference (a missed one fails to compile, not silently). It lands scripted in one motion at a quiet moment, because it touches about 200 files and will conflict with in-flight PRs."),
          li(text: "**Done:** no symbol spells a machine's current or past name."),
        ]),
      ]),
      li_blocks(blocks: [
        p(text: "**P6a-P6c, generalizations** (medium each; not on the path to the first flip)."),
        ul(items: [
          li(text: "**Scope:** R2 `fleet_host_record_for`; R3 the host-keyed map (`PerHostReplaceBudgetState` and its siblings); R4's policy columns on `HostEnrollmentIntent` (apply mode, reach admission, arrival standing grant, run-scoped federation names), with `arrival_subject` and the mtcollins1 federation moved onto them. D2's re-keying of per-machine fact declarations happens table by table as each rule is lifted. Delivered elsewhere and consumed here: the derived `RunnerHostSpec` and the fleet-wide access template (cool-lark-40), and the host-generic Redfish boot-once (R5, smart-crane-730)."),
          li(text: "**Acceptance:** each absorbed branch or leaf is deleted, not wrapped. A fixture host outside srv1-srv4 gets a real answer where it used to get the silent zero (budget, width, overhead). A second arrival row (srv13/bobo's) admits against its own grant."),
          li(text: "**Done:** the 4.2 regex over the touched modules finds no `== operator_host_` arm."),
        ]),
      ]),
      li_blocks(blocks: [
        p(text: "**P7a-P7d, live modes** (medium each). The first three come before the srv4 flip; P7d comes before the first retirement."),
        ul(items: [
          li(text: "**P7a, hostname:** a fleet-converge mode run from a peer host. It re-adopts the baseline (`gunbc.host.host_identity_adopt`), then sets and reads back the hostname through `host_identity_converge_from_base`. It is needed because a host's own fleet-converge job is pinned to its label."),
          li(text: "**P7b, secrets:** a shadow copy. It creates `bmc-<new>-admin`, copies the latest version, and adds the same IAM cells, all additive, extending `gunbc.auth.gcp_iam_converge` `GcpIamEffect`."),
          li(text: "**P7c, known_hosts and Tailscale:** the existing `fleet_host_key_scan_wet` and `fleet_host_key_enroll_wet` wired as a mode; a Tailscale name mode that reads first, sets with `tailscale set --hostname` and reads back with `tailscale status --json` (D8)."),
          li(text: "**P7d, retirement:** a JIT offline-registration sweep for the old name."),
          li(text: "**Acceptance:** each mode is a dry plan plus a wet apply with independent read-back. Its first wet run is against srv4's S2 shadow artifacts and is a no-op re-run on the second pass."),
          li(text: "**Done:** S2 and S3 for srv4 need no hand step except the console's OAuth edit, which srv4 does not have."),
        ]),
      ]),
      li_blocks(blocks: [
        p(text: "**P8, flip srv4 to fox** (small diff plus a live window)."),
        ul(items: [
          li(text: "**Depends on:** P1-P5 and P7a-P7c; cool-lark-40's `gunbc-runner` cutover being ready for srv4; srv4's S1 (P3) and S2 complete."),
          li(text: "**Scope:** the diff moves srv4's row from `next_name` to `name` and regenerates the workflows. Nothing else changes, by D2 and P5. The window runs section 5.2 S3."),
          li_blocks(blocks: [
            p(text: "**Acceptance, every item read back live:**"),
            ul(items: [
              li(text: "`hostname -s` is fox."),
              li(text: "JIT registrations under label fox are online and complete v2-bootstrap jobs."),
              li(text: "A fleet-converge run with `host: fox` succeeds."),
              li(text: "`bmc_fan_converge` reads `bmc-fox-admin`."),
              li(text: "The known_hosts anchor connects to fox."),
              li(text: "fox resolves on the LAN zone, and the Tailscale name is fox."),
              li(text: "v2-bootstrap stays green across the window."),
            ]),
          ]),
          li(text: "**Done:** srv4 serves CI as fox, and its S4 list of old artifacts is written down. Anything that broke is fixed at its derivation in a follow-up to P4 or P6, not in the flip."),
        ]),
      ]),
      li_blocks(blocks: [
        p(text: "**P9.x, the other flips** (small each). Order: srv3 (after R5 and P4), srv2, srv1, mtcollins1. Then the hosts whose names are already drawn: srv9-srv12, mtjade1, host-183527, host-3dde7f, host-6ce85c; srv14/butch with cool-lark-40; srv15/bobo after smart-crane-730."),
        ul(items: [
          li(text: "**Acceptance:** P8's checklist for that host, plus the host-specific extras: srv1's pinned jobs run under its new label, srv1 and srv2's OAuth URIs are edited in the console and read back (D8), and mtcollins1's next image build carries its label."),
          li(text: "**Done:** every machine's identity is its drawn (or legacy H11) name."),
        ]),
      ]),
      li_blocks(blocks: [
        p(text: "**P10.x, retire per host** (small each, piece by piece, D10)."),
        ul(items: [
          li(text: "**Scope:** retire each old artifact once nothing reads it: secrets (disable, then delete), known_hosts rows, offline registrations (P7d), OAuth URIs, the old Tailscale name."),
          li(text: "**Acceptance:** a green run of each artifact's consumer after its removal."),
          li(text: "**Done:** no live artifact carries an old name."),
        ]),
      ]),
      li_blocks(blocks: [
        p(text: "**P11, the wall** (large, mechanical; any time after P5, and it is what keeps the result from regressing)."),
        ul(items: [
          li(text: "**Scope:** `HostIdentity` becomes `sole_constructor`, minted only by `admit_fleet_machines`. Every `as HostIdentity` cast and identity literal moves to the admission or to fixture identities minted through it."),
          li(text: "**Acceptance:** W3, fixture source with `\"srv1\" as HostIdentity` refused by the compiler, plus the production positive control."),
          li(text: "**Done:** `git grep -n 'as HostIdentity'` finds only the admission and fixture minting."),
        ]),
      ]),
    ]),
    p(text: "Before each PR, search the open PRs that touch its files: `gh pr list --json files` filtered by path. At this revision: #16058 and #16246 touch the `runner_host_*` files, #16035 and #15978 touch `runner_host_file_converge`, #15221 touches `runner_connectivity_recovery`, and #15287 touches the mtcollins1 boot approval."),
    h2(text: "7. Proposed draws (receipts for the operator; not applied)"),
    p(text: "Drawn 2026-11-10 with fresh 12-digit entropy. The names were computed by a transcription of `draw_human_name` (first-part corpus 432 entries, last-part 24), which reproduces all nine recorded draws exactly. Each draw was taken against every existing selector form and against the draws before it. The real allocator re-draws each receipt in P2's witness, so a mismatch reds there instead of standing."),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "srv1: entropy 458621672034, forms ricky / ricky-energy / ricky-dexter-energy, so **ricky**."),
      li(text: "srv2: entropy 905841313466, forms cubby / cubby-coded / cubby-vincent-coded, so **cubby**."),
      li(text: "srv3: entropy 710002629885, forms bruno / bruno-girlboss / bruno-wes-girlboss, so **bruno**."),
      li(text: "srv4: entropy 615953933451, forms fox / fox-core / fox-ang-core, so **fox**. This is a redraw at the operator's request (D3): the first draw, 434002117982, gave erik, which sounds like mtjade1's eric, and is withdrawn."),
      li(text: "mtcollins1: entropy 374329216198, forms connor / connor-slaps / connor-nicolas-slaps, so **connor**."),
      li(text: "**Order matters.** The witness re-draws each row against the rows before it, so a converted row stays at the end of the receipt list, in draw order, rather than replacing srv1's row in place (where nothing would precede it)."),
    ]),

    h2(text: "8. Decisions (operator rulings, 2026-11-10)"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**D1, accepted.** Deriving the hostname from the identity is fine as long as the derivation is modeled. The identity carries the typed drawn name, and the hostname is its declared rendering (`human_name_canonical_hostname`), never a parse of an opaque string. This supersedes `gunbc.hostname_allocation` `gunbc_hostname_allocation_scope_disposition`, which P2 rewrites."),
      li(text: "**D2, no hard-coded per-host declarations.** The operator's words: they are mini forks, and wanting to write code that way means the rule is not generalized well. So the target is not to rename `operator_host_srv1` and the declarations named after a host. It is that rule code names no machine at all. A per-host branch or a host-prefixed declaration in a rule is generalized (R1-R4). A fact about one machine (its captures, its census, its first contact) is a row in a table keyed by `HostIdentity`, not a declaration named after the machine. What remains is the machine rows themselves. The acceptance test for the whole program is that a rename edits one row."),
      li(text: "**D3, accepted, with srv4 redrawn:** srv1 ricky, srv2 cubby, srv3 bruno, srv4 fox, mtcollins1 connor (section 7)."),
      li(text: "**D4, secret ids keyed by name, and renames made cheap.** Everything downstream of the name is consolidated in this program, not just the five hosts' literals: the 2.3 derivations, the R1-R4 generalizations, and the section 5 modes, so that the live part of a rename (shadow secrets, known_hosts, hostname, Tailscale name, runner labels) is run by modes rather than by hand. W2 is the in-tree check of that."),
      li(text: "**D5, accepted:** srv16's reserved row is deleted in P2."),
      li(text: "**D6, accepted:** `chassis-srvN` becomes opaque (`chassis-NN`) in P2."),
      li(text: "**D7, accepted:** historical observations keep the spelling that was observed."),
      li_blocks(blocks: [
        p(text: "**D8, accepted, and where each change is made.**"),
        ul(items: [
          li(text: "**OAuth redirect URIs.** These are in the Google Cloud console for project `gunbc-tracker` (number 433089409875), under Auth Platform > Clients, on clients tracker-web-test and tracker-web-stage. The desired URIs are already derived from the host identity by `gunbc.auth.tracker_web_oauth_client` `tracker_web_oauth_public_redirect_uri`, so they follow the flip. The console edit is a manual obligation that `gunbc.auth.google_workspace_admin_convergence` models and reads back. Only srv1 and srv2 carry these URIs."),
          li(text: "**Tailscale.** ACL convergence exists (`gunbc.tailscale_acl_emit`, `gunbc.tailscale_acl_phase2_credential`), and `tailscale serve` is modeled (`gunbc.tailscale_serve_scope`). Nothing sets or reads a machine's Tailscale name: `git grep -nE 'tailscale (up|set)|--hostname'` returns 0. P7c adds that mode, which sets the name through `tailscale set --hostname` and reads it back through `tailscale status --json`, keyed by the derived name. Whether a Tailscale name follows an OS hostname change on its own is not established here, so the mode reads before it writes."),
        ]),
      ]),
      li(text: "**D9, srv4 first,** then the others once srv4 works (section 5.3). Each host's `gunbc-runner` cutover stays in the same window as its flip, sequenced with cool-lark-40."),
      li(text: "**D10, no fixed soak.** Old artifacts are retired piece by piece as each is shown unread, and breakage is fixed where it arises (S4)."),
      li(text: "**D11 (open), how a fact row names its machine.** D2 asks that a rename edit one row. Today a row about one machine names it through the symbol `operator_host_srv4`, and once srv4 is fox that symbol is a nickname. Option (a): rename the symbols at each flip. This is mechanical and the compiler catches a missed reference, but a rename is then no longer one row. Option (b): give each machine a stable opaque handle (`machine_01` ...), as `gpu_board_NN` already are, with the name only in the row's name field. That is a one-time mechanical migration (P5), and from then on a rename is one row. Option (c): key facts by board serial. That is rejected, because a board swap would orphan facts about the machine's role. Recommendation: (b)."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "9. What this does not claim"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "The census is a candidate set from name search and source inspection at one revision. A site it missed is added to section 4 when found; this list does not rule one out."),
      li(text: "Live state was not read in this lane: live hostnames, Tailscale names, which BMC secrets exist, and router names all come from the corpus. S1 and S2 read them before acting."),
      li(text: "The draw names were computed by a transcription of the allocator, not the allocator itself. P2's witness is the execution that confirms them."),
    ]),
  ]
}

data fleet_machine_naming_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly,
  slug: "fleet-machine-naming",
  title: "Fleet machine naming: one name per machine, every other name derived",
  body: fleet_machine_naming_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Every machine in gunbc.fleet.fleet_host_identity is one admitted row whose identity is its rendered name; gunbc_fleet_hostname_allocations holds only draw receipts; HostIdentity is sole_constructor with W1, W2 and W3 enrolled; srv1-srv4, mtcollins1 and the already-drawn hosts have flipped and retired their old names (S4); and the R2-R4 generalizations have landed or been recorded with their triggers (R5 is smart-crane-730's). This plan then deletes.") },
}
